{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7905","id":5217382774,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNvrxdg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7905","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7905.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7905.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7905","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7905/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7905/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7905/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/a3f6b1e0a488c5fc9332fd10768a4e5186bb9362","number":7905,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"id: server-to-server file transfer (send) — #5345","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements #5345 (transport + CLI/REPL slice of #1794, design #4975): a user-initiated, single-file copy from one running `id` server to another, performed by the source server with its own identity.\n\n## What\n\n- **`transfer` module** (`pkgs/id/src/transfer.rs`): the one server-side transfer interface shared by every surface. Conflict pre-check over the meta protocol before any bytes move; bytes-before-name via the existing `push_and_name` (blobs push, then name registration, success only after the destination confirms); idempotent re-send (same hash already registered → `already_present`, nothing pushed); conflicts refuse by default, explicit replacement archives the existing destination file under `<name>.archive.<unix-ts>` first; the source is never modified.\n- **Meta protocol** (`/iroh-meta/3`, append-only per the compatibility rule): new `MetaRequest::Send` (discriminant 14, included in `is_write` so the source authorizes the initiating user with the existing write gate) and `MetaResponse::Send` receipt (discriminant 15). `wire_format_is_pinned` extended. `MetaProtocol` gains an optional endpoint; `id serve` and `LocalNode` wire the node's own endpoint in, so the destination authorizes the *source server's* node ID and records it as the copy's `origin` with its first-write `created` time (#4973/#5191 contract).\n- **CLI**: `id send SOURCE_NODE_ID NAME --to DEST_NODE_ID [--as DEST_NAME] [--replace]`.\n- **REPL**: `send [--replace] <NAME> <DEST_NODE> [DEST_NAME]`, sharing the same meta request.\n\nThe web adapter stays #5346 and can call the same module/request; it is out of scope here.\n\n## Tests\n\nTwo-Iroh-node integration tests in `transfer.rs` (ephemeral `LocalNode`s, real QUIC + blobs + meta protocols):\n- send copies the blob, registers the name, and stamps the source server as `origin` with an upload time; source contents unchanged (copy, not move)\n- re-send is idempotent (`already_present`)\n- conflict refuses by default and changes nothing; `--replace` archives the old file under an archive name and registers the new hash\n- a destination whose write policy does not allowlist the source denies the send and gains no name\n\nPlus the extended wire-format pin test for the new protocol variants.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check` in `pkgs/id`: pass\n- Targeted tests: `cargo test --lib -- transfer:: wire_format_is_pinned protocol:: meta_client:: fileops:: cli:: local::` in pkgs/id — all pass (4 two-node transfer tests, wire pin, CLI command-list coverage incl. README + module doc)\n\nCloses #5345\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796780647&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7905&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7905&signature=12ca55d4bde13284f527de63bb12d67509be362f975894f193b0ec899da210e9\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7905?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T01:44:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T23:38:26Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T23:38:04Z","merged